<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|letter>

<\body>
  <\letter-header>
    <\address>
      Analytical Engine Society

      12 Difference Street

      London
    </address>

    <letter-date|1 October 2026>

    <\destination>
      Mr. Charles Babbage

      1 Dorset Street

      London
    </destination>
  </letter-header>

  <opening|Dear Mr. Babbage,>

  This letter exercises the letter style: the address of the sender and the
  date flushed to the right, the address of the recipient on the left,
  the opening, the body, the closing and the signature, followed by the
  copies and the enclosures.

  The body of a letter is set as ordinary paragraphs. This second paragraph
  is long enough to wrap onto a second line, so that the measure of the
  letter style and the justification of its lines can be checked.

  <closing|Yours sincerely,>

  <signature|Ada Lovelace>

  <cc|Mary Somerville>

  <encl|Notes on the Analytical Engine>
</body>

<initial|<\collection>
</collection>>
